<title>SOUTH AFRICA: C.G. Smith Foods lifts yr shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>C.G. Smith Foods lifts yr shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)     525.1	 vs    414.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   176.5	 vs    141.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	     639.8	 vs    392.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   1,717.6	 vs    1,148.0</p>
<p>    Tax			   494.1	 vs    401.6</p>
<p>    Abnormal items	    253.5 gain  vs    33.2 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		 18,665.6	 vs    16,775.6</p>
<p>    Share of associates'     38.4	 vs    15.5</p>
<p>Div payable January 10</p>
<p>on register December 6</p>
<p>Full name: C.G. Smith Foods Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said the abnormal profit arose mainly out of the profit on a change of interest in subsidiaries, associates and other investments as well as the profit on the disposal of land and buildings.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
